{"loc":"TABRISI:2:180#2","rows":[{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["الْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"Tabrisi rejects abrogating the certain Qur'anic rule with a report that, even if sound, establishes only probability.","anchor":"فقد أبعد لأن الخبر لو سلم من كل قدح لكان يقتضي الظن ولا يجوز أن ينسخ كتاب الله تعالى"},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["الْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If the no-bequest-for-an-heir report is accepted despite criticism of its transmitter, it can specify the verse: an heir may receive a bequest up to one third, not beyond it.","anchor":"لخصصنا عموم الآية وحملناها على أنه لا وصية لوارث بما يزيد على الثلث"},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِينَ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"Consensus that a bequest is not obligatory does not prove abrogation, since a recommended and encouraged act need not be obligatory.","anchor":"الإجماع إنما هو على أنها لا تفيد الفرض وذلك لا يمنع من كونها مندوبا إليها مرغبا فيها"},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["الْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو جعفر","stance":"reports","claim":"Asked whether a bequest to an heir is permissible, Abu Jaʿfar answered yes and recited this verse.","anchor":"عن أبي جعفر عليه السلام أنه سئل هل تجوز الوصية للوارث فقال: نعم وتلا هذه الآية"},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["وَٱلْأَقْرَبِينَ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAlī says that dying without a bequest for close relatives who do not inherit ends one's deeds in disobedience.","anchor":"السكوني عن أبي عبد الله عن أبيه عن علي ع قال: من لم يوص عند موته لذوي قرابته"},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["الْوَصِيَّةُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A report attributed to the Prophet says that one who dies without a will dies a death of the pre-Islamic age.","anchor":"النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال:
" من مات بغير وصية مات ميتة جاهلية ""},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["الْوَصِيَّةُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet is reported to call a person's failure to make a sound will before death a deficiency in character and intellect.","anchor":"النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال:
" من مات بغير وصية مات ميتة جاهلية "
وعنه عليه السلام أنه قال:"},{"verses":["2:180"],"words":["الْوَصِيَّةُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu ʿAbd Allāh says a Muslim should not go to sleep without keeping his will beneath his head.","anchor":"أبي عبد الله عليه السلام أنه قال:
" ما ينبغي لامرىء مسلم أن يبيت إلا ووصيته تحت رأسه ""}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185","rows":[{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās says that breaking the fast while traveling is a firm obligation, not merely a concession.","anchor":"عن ابن عباس أنه قال: الإفطار في إلسفر عزيمة."},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿAbd Allāh compares fasting during Ramadan travel to breaking the fast while at home.","anchor":"عن أبي عبد الله أنه قال: الصائم في شهر رمضان في السفر كالمفطر فيه في الحضور"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿAbd Allāh says he would not perform the funeral prayer for a man who died fasting during a journey.","anchor":"وعنه ع قال: لو أن رجلا مات صائما في السفر لما صليت عليه"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet says a traveler breaks the fast and shortens prayer, except when traveling to hunt or to commit disobedience to God.","anchor":"صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: " من سافر أفطر وقصر إلا أن يكون رجلا سفره إلى صيد"},{"verses":["2:184","2:185"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-ʿAyyāshī transmits from Muḥammad ibn Muslim that the Prophet first broke a Ramadan journey fast at Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm, ordered the people to break theirs, and called those who continued disobedient; the name persisted until his death.","anchor":"إلى محمد بن مسلم عن أبي عبد الله قال: لم يكن رسول الله يصوم في السفر"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Most scholars take the pronoun in this phrase to refer to fasting: those able to fast initially could either fast without expiation or break the fast and feed a poor person per day.","anchor":"الهاء: يعود إلى الصوم عند أكثر أهل العلم"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan and Abū Muslim instead take the pronoun to refer to the ransom or feeding payment.","anchor":"الهاء يعود إلى الفداء عن الحسن وأبي مسلم"},{"verses":["2:184","2:185"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās and al-Shaʿbī understand the phrase to cover all people under an initial choice between fasting and feeding, later abrogated by the command to fast when present for Ramadan.","anchor":"أنه ساير الناس كما قدمنا ذكره من التخيير والنسخ بعده وهو قول ابن عباس والشعبي"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan and ʿAṭāʾ say the original concession covered pregnant and nursing women and the very old; the pregnant and nursing were later excluded, while the elderly person's concession remained.","anchor":"أن هذه الرخصة كانت للحوامل والمراضع والشيخ الفاني ثم نسخ من الآية الحامل والمرضع وبقي الشيخ الكبير"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddī says this concerns people who formerly could fast but became unable, so there is no abrogation.","anchor":"أن معناه وعلى الذين كانوا يطيقونه ثم صاروا بحيث لا يطيقونه ولا نسخ فيه عن السدي"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وعلى الذين يطيقونه"],"type":"law","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"A report from Abū ʿAbd Allāh says that an older person or someone afflicted by thirst after previously being able to fast owes one mudd of food daily.","anchor":"رواه بعض أصحابنا عن أبي عبد الله أن معناه وعلى الذين كانوا يطيقون الصوم ثم أصابهم كبر أو عطاش"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فدية طعام مسكين"],"type":"law","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Through ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm, al-Ṣādiq says a person who missed Ramadan through illness, recovered, but did not make it up before the next Ramadan owes both make-up fasting and one mudd of food per missed day.","anchor":"بإسناده عن الصادق ع وعلى الذين يطيقونه فدية من مرض في شهر رمضان فأفطر ثم صح"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فدية طعام مسكين"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Iraqis set the fidya at half a ṣāʿ per day, al-Shāfiʿī at one mudd, and the Imāmī position at two mudd for the able person or one mudd if unable.","anchor":"اختلف في مقدار الفدية فقال أهل العراق: نصف صاع عن كل يوم وقال الشافعي: عن كل يوم مد"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فمن تطوع خيرا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عطاء","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAṭāʾ and Ṭāwūs interpret voluntary extra good as feeding more than one poor person.","anchor":"معناه من أطعم أكثر من مسكين واحد عن عطاء وطاوس"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فمن تطوع خيرا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid interprets it as giving one poor person more than the adequate amount, beyond half a ṣāʿ.","anchor":"أطعم المسكين الواحد أكثر من قدر الكفاية حتى يزيده على نصف صاع عن مجاهد"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فمن تطوع خيرا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās reconciles the preceding views: voluntary good means increasing the amount of food given.","anchor":"قول ابن عباس: من تطوع بزيادة الإطعام"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فمن تطوع خيرا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan gives another reading: the phrase means doing good in combining religious practices.","anchor":"قيل: معناه من عمل برا في جمع الدين عن الحسن"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["فمن تطوع خيرا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الزهري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zuhrī understands the phrase as fasting in addition to paying the fidya.","anchor":"وقيل من صام مع الفدية عن الزهري"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وأن تصوموا خير لكم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The comparison that fasting is better than fidya applied while paying fidya was permitted; after abrogation, breaking the fast is not lawful for those required to fast.","anchor":"وكان هذا مع جواز الفدية فأما بعد النسخ فلا يجوز أن يقال الصوم خير من الفدية"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["وأن تصوموا خير لكم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation says fasting is better for someone able to fast, and earns a greater reward than expiation for one unable to fast.","anchor":"وقيل معناه الصوم خير لمطيقه وأفضل ثوابا من التكفير لمن أفطر بالعجز"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["إن كنتم تعلمون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The closing condition is also read as meaning: if you know which deeds are best.","anchor":"وقيل: إن كنتم تعلمون أفضل أعمالكم"},{"verses":["2:184"],"words":["الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Tabrisi takes the wording to indicate that capacity exists before the act is performed.","anchor":"دلالة على أن الاستطاعة قبل الفعل"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#2","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو بكر عن عاصم","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Bakr from ʿĀṣim reads ولتكملوا with a doubled consonant; the other readers use the lighter form.","anchor":"قرأ أبو بكر عن عاصم ولتكملوا بالتشديد والباقون لتكملوا بالتخفيف"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["ٱلْيُسْرَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو جعفر","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Jaʿfar reads العسر and اليسر with the heavier articulation; the remaining readers use the lighter articulation.","anchor":"وقرأ أبو جعفر العسر واليسر بالتثقيل فيهما والباقون بالتخفيف"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The reading ولتكملوا is supported by the Qur'anic wording اليوم أكملت لكم دينكم.","anchor":"ولتكملوا قوله:
اليوم أكملت لكم دينكم","mentions":["5:3"]},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"النابغة","stance":"reports","claim":"The other form is supported by the interchangeability of the فعل and أفعل patterns; al-Nābigha's verse uses كملت in this sense.","anchor":"النابغة.
فكملت مائة منها حمامتها وأسرعت حسبة في ذلك العدد"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Shahr is the familiar word for month, pluralized as أشهر for a small number and شهور for larger numbers; its root concerns appearing, as the crescent makes a month known.","anchor":"الشهر معروف وجمعه في القلة أشهر وفي الكثرة شهور وأصله من اشتهاره بالهلال"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The root شهَر also means to make something manifest or draw it out; a broad, heavy she-camel is also called شهيرة.","anchor":"شهرت الحديث: أظهرته وشهرت السيف"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ramadan derives from intense heat striking sand; the months were named for their seasons, and Ramadan coincided with hot weather. Its plural includes رمضانات.","anchor":"وأصل رمضان من الرمض، وهو شدة وقع الشمس على الرمل"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid reports that Ramadan is one of God's names and advises saying شهر رمضان because one cannot know what Ramadan is.","anchor":"عن مجاهد:
" لا تقل رمضان ولكن قل شهر رمضان"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A Prophetic report promises forgiveness of prior sins to whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and expectation of reward.","anchor":"عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال:
" من صام رمضان إيمانا واحتسابا"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#3","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another proposed etymology says Ramadan was named because it burns away sins.","anchor":"سمي رمضان لأنه يرمض الذنوب أي يحرقها"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["ٱلْقُرْءَانَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qur'an is connected to gathering: Arabs said a she-camel had not gathered her womb around a foetus, and reading gathers letters together.","anchor":"والقرآن أصله الجمع لقولهم ما قرأت الناقة سلأ قط"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَٱلْفُرْقَانِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Furqān means that which distinguishes truth from falsehood.","anchor":"والفرقان الذي يفرق بين الحق والباطل"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Irāda has an original wāw, as related forms such as rāwadahu and rād; it means seeking the intended object and is its cause.","anchor":"والإرادة أصلها الواو لأنك تقول راودته على أن يفعل كذا"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["ٱلْيُسْرَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Yusr is the opposite of hardship and has related senses of wealth, the left hand, and a group sharing a camel in maysir; its root is ease.","anchor":"واليسر ضد العسر واليسار الغنى والسعة واليسار اليد اليسرى واليسر الجماعة يجتمعون على الجزور"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["ٱلْعُسْرَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The root of ʿusr is hardness; aʿsar can mean left-handed, and aʿsara can mean becoming poor, with ease as its opposite.","anchor":"وأصل العسر الصلابة يقال عسر الشيء عسرا ورجل أعسر يعمل بشماله وأعسر الرجل إذا افتقر"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The verbs كمل الشيء, أكمله, and كمّله all mean that something was completed or brought to completion.","anchor":"ويقال كمل الشيء وأكملته وكملته أي تممته"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"شهر رمضان may be nominative as the predicate of an omitted subject, as apposition to الصيام, or as a subject whose relative clause or description supplies an omitted predicate.","anchor":"شهر رمضان في ارتفاعه ثلاثة أوجه"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ramadan does not take nunation because it is definite and ends in the augmented alif and nūn resembling the feminine dual endings.","anchor":"لا ينصرف رمضان للتعريف وزيادة الألف والنون"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In Arabic, شهر رمضان can also be accusative as the object of an implied command to fast, or in apposition to أياما.","anchor":"ويجوز في العربية شهر رمضان بالنصب من وجهين"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["هُدًۭى لِّلنَّاسِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"هدى is accusative as a circumstantial expression, meaning that the Qur'an guides people.","anchor":"في موضع النصب على الحال"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ ٱلشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Here الشهر is an adverbial time expression meaning the person is resident in the town during Ramadan, not an object; otherwise a traveler who witnesses the month would also have to fast.","anchor":"فالشهر ينتصب على أنه ظرف لا على أنه مفعول به"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَلْيَصُمْهُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The attached pronoun in فليصمه is permissible through syntactic extension after الشهر has already been used adverbially.","anchor":"الاتساع وقع فيه بعد أن استعمل ظرفا"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍۢ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preposition in على سفر coordinates with the adjective مريضا because it has the sense of the noun مسافرا.","anchor":"وإنما عطف الظرف على الاسم"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#4","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍۢ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The same coordination of an adverbial phrase with an adjective appears in Yunus 10:12, where lying, sitting, and standing are coordinated forms.","anchor":"دعانا لجنبه أو قاعدا أو قائما","mentions":["10:12"]},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ treats ولتكملوا as a coordinated sentence with an omitted clause, approximately: this was prescribed or intended so that you complete the count; he compares 6:75.","anchor":"عطف جملة على جملة لأن بعده محذوفا","mentions":["6:75"]},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjāj coordinates the phrase with the understood meaning of God's willing ease: He has made matters easy for you so that you complete the count.","anchor":"عطفا على تأويل محذوف ودل عليه ما تقدم من الكلام"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The first grammatical analysis is illustrated by the wording in 6:75: God showed Abraham the kingdom so that he might become certain.","anchor":"إبراهيم ملكوت السماوات والأرض وليكون من الموقنين","mentions":["6:75"]},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A cited poem illustrates coordination with the inferred sense of an omitted part of the preceding statement; al-Zajjāj gives this analysis, while the first is al-Farrāʾ's.","anchor":"بادت وغير آيهن مع البلى إلا رواكد جمرهن هباء"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The counted days are identified as Ramadan, and it is singled out for fasting because of its special virtues: the Qur'an, on which religion and faith depend, was sent down in it.","anchor":"هذه الأيام المعدودات شهر رمضان"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أُنزِلَ فِيهِ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās, Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, al-Ḥasan, and Qatāda say the whole Qur'an descended to the lowest heaven on Laylat al-Qadr, then came to the Prophet piecemeal over twenty years; this is also transmitted from Abū ʿAbd Allāh.","anchor":"عن ابن عباس وسعيد بن جبير والحسن وقتادة وهو المروي عن أبي عبد الله"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أُنزِلَ فِيهِ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Isḥāq says the Qur'an's revelation began on Laylat al-Qadr in Ramadan.","anchor":"ابتدأ إنزاله في ليلة القدر من شهر رمضان عن ابن إسحاق"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أُنزِلَ فِيهِ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddī, transmitting from Ibn ʿAbbās, says the year's needed revelation descended together to the lowest heaven on Laylat al-Qadr, then was sent down in stages over months and days.","anchor":"في الشهور والأيام عن السدي بسنده إلى ابن عباس"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أُنزِلَ فِيهِ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A report through Abū Dharr attributes to the Prophet that Abraham's scriptures were sent down on the third of Ramadan.","anchor":"أبي ذر الغفاري عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال:
" أنزلت صحف إبراهيم لثلاث مضين"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#5","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أُنزِلَ فِيهِ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"In the report's continuation, Abraham's scriptures are dated to the first or third night of Ramadan; Moses' Torah to the sixth, Jesus' Gospel to the thirteenth, David's Psalms to the eighteenth, and the Qur'an to the twenty-fourth. Al-ʿAyyāshī transmits this from al-Ṣādiq and his forefathers, ending with the Prophet.","anchor":"لأربع وعشرين من شهر رمضان وهذا بعينه رواه العياشي عن أبي عبد الله عن آبائه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["أُنزِلَ فِيهِ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation takes أنزل فيه القرآن to mean that the Qur'an was revealed concerning the obligation and prescription of fasting, with فيه meaning concerning its prescription.","anchor":"أنه أنزل في فرضه وإيجاب صومه على الخلق"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["هُدًۭى لِّلنَّاسِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Qur'an is guidance for people, directing them to the kinds of knowledge they are obligated to acquire, and its signs are proofs of guidance.","anchor":"دالا لهم على ما كلفوه من العلوم"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["هُدًۭى لِّلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّنَٰتٍۢ مِّنَ ٱلْهُدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās says the first guidance is guidance away from error, while the second means clarification of the lawful and unlawful.","anchor":"وقيل المراد بالهدى الأول الهدى من الضلالة وبالثاني بيان الحلال والحرام عن ابن عباس"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["هُدًۭى لِّلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّنَٰتٍۢ مِّنَ ٱلْهُدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الأصم","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Aṣamm and al-Qāḍī say the first guidance is the initial knowledge required of people; the second comprises accounts of prophets, their laws, and histories, which are known through the Qur'an.","anchor":"وقيل أراد بأول ما كلف من العلم وبالثاني ما يشتمل عليه من الأنبياء وشرائعهم وأخبارهم لأنها لا تدرك إلا بالقرآن عن الأصم والقاضي"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#6","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَٱلْفُرْقَانِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Furqān is that which separates truth from falsehood.","anchor":"أي ومما يفرق بين الحق والباطل"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["ٱلْقُرْءَانُ وَٱلْفُرْقَانِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿAbd Allāh distinguishes the Qur'an as the book as a whole from the Furqān, the decisive rulings that must be followed.","anchor":"عن أبي عبد الله ع أنه قال: القرآن جملة الكتاب"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"In a sermon reported by al-Bāqir through al-Ḥasan ibn Maḥbūb, Abū Ayyūb, and Abū al-Ward, the Prophet describes Ramadan's night better than a thousand months, obligatory fast, and voluntary night prayer worth seventy months' prayers; good deeds equal obligatory deeds elsewhere and an obligatory deed equals seventy. He calls it a month of patience, mutual aid, and increased provision; feeding a faster brings emancipation and forgiveness, even a sip of milk, water, or a few dates suffices, and easing a servant's work eases one's reckoning. He describes its beginning as mercy, middle as forgiveness, and end as answered prayer and release from fire; he urges testimony, asking for needs and Paradise, and seeking refuge from Hell.","anchor":"خطب رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم الناس في آخر جمعة من شعبان"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"سلمان الفارسي","stance":"reports","claim":"Salman al-Fārisī's version urges four practices: the testimony of faith and seeking forgiveness please God, while asking for Paradise and refuge from Hell are indispensable.","anchor":"وفي رواية سلمان الفارسي
" فاستكثروا فيه من أربع خصال"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#7","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet is reported to say that a fasting person's sleep is worship, silence is glorification, prayer is answered, and deeds are multiplied.","anchor":"وقال رسول الله نوم الصائم عبادة وصمته تسبيح ودعاؤه مستجاب وعمله مضاعف"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ ٱلشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The stronger reading is that one who is present in town and not away during Ramadan must fast the whole month; الشهر is definite for the known month.","anchor":"فمن شهد منكم المصر وحضر ولم يغب في الشهر والألف واللام في الشهر للعهد والمراد به شهر رمضان"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ ٱلشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو جعفر","stance":"reports","claim":"Asked about the wording, Abū Jaʿfar says it plainly means whoever witnesses Ramadan should fast it, while whoever travels in it should break the fast; this report is from Zurāra.","anchor":"ما رواه زرارة عن أبي جعفر أنه قال لما سئل عن هذه ما أبينها لمن عقلها قال من شهد رمضان فليصمه"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ ٱلشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAlī, Ibn ʿAbbās, Mujāhid, and other exegetes say that entering Ramadan while resident obliges fasting its entire month.","anchor":"وقد روي أيضا عن علي وابن عباس ومجاهد وجماعة من المفسرين أنهم قالوا من شهد الشهر بأن دخل عليه الشهر"},{"verses":["2:185","2:184"],"words":["فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ ٱلشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A second reading takes the phrase to mean a legally responsible person who is resident when the month arrives must fast that month; it abrogates the earlier choice of fasting or fidya, since recitation order does not determine order of revelation. Tabrisi prefers the first reading.","anchor":"من شاهد منهم الشهر مقيما مكلفا فليصم الشهر بعينه وهذا نسخ للتخيير بين الصوم والفدية"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["مَرِيضًا"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The qualifying illness is one that makes a person fear an extreme worsening of the illness.","anchor":"وحد المرض الذي يوجب الإفطار ما يخاف الإنسان معه الزيادة المفرطة في مرضه"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["مَرِيضًا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو عبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Baṣīr reports that al-Ṣādiq leaves assessment of illness to the person: if weak, break the fast; if strong enough, fast, whatever the illness.","anchor":"روى أبو بصير قال سألت أبا عبد الله عن حد المرض الذي على صاحبه فيه الإفطار قال هو مؤتمن عليه مفوض إليه"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["مَرِيضًا"],"type":"law","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Another transmitted definition is any illness that prevents someone from standing for as long as a prayer; al-Ḥasan holds this, and jurists disagree.","anchor":"وروي أيضا أن ذلك كل مرض لا يقدر معه على القيام بمقدار زمان صلاته وبه قال الحسن وفي ذلك اختلاف بين الفقهاء"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍۢ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In the Imāmī school, a journey allowing a fast to be broken is permitted or devotional and measures eight farsakhs, twenty-four miles; al-Shāfiʿī requires sixteen farsakhs and Abū Ḥanīfa twenty-four.","anchor":"وأما السفر الذي يوجب الإفطار عندنا فما كان مباحا أو طاعة وكانت المسافة ثمانية فراسخ أربعة وعشرين ميلا"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَعِدَّةٌۭ مِّنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ"],"type":"law","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan and others require making up missed days immediately once the sick person recovers or the traveler returns.","anchor":"فقال الحسن وجماعة هي على التضييق إذا برىء المريض أو قدم المسافر"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَعِدَّةٌۭ مِّنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ"],"type":"law","speaker":"أبو حنيفة","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Ḥanīfa allows make-up days to be delayed; the Imāmī school sets the period before the next Ramadan, allows consecutive or separate days, and prefers consecutive days.","anchor":"وقال أبو حنيفة موسع فيها وعندنا موقت بما بين رمضانين وتجوز متتابعة ومتفرقة والتتابع أفضل"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["فَعِدَّةٌۭ مِّنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If make-up fasting is delayed until another Ramadan arrives, fidya is due along with the make-up fast; al-Shāfiʿī agrees.","anchor":"فإن فرط حتى لحقه رمضان آخر لزمه الفدية والقضاء وبه قال الشافعي"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ بِكُمُ ٱلْيُسْرَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God wills ease by granting the sick and traveler a dispensation not to fast during those circumstances.","anchor":"أي في الرخصة للمريض والمسافر إذ لم يوجب الصوم عليهما"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ بِكُمُ ٱلْيُسْرَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation takes God's willing ease to apply to all human affairs.","anchor":"وقيل يريد الله بكم اليسر في جميع أموركم"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلَا يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ بِكُمُ ٱلْعُسْرَ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"Tabrisi uses the verse against the compulsion doctrine: God wills ease in some human acts, does not will hardship in others, and therefore does not will imposing the impossible.","anchor":"وفيه دلالة على بطلان قول المجبرة لأنه بين أن في أفعال المكلفين ما يريده سبحانه وهو اليسر"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:185#8","rows":[{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The completion is the make-up of the days missed through illness or travel, fasted after recovery or return; alternatively, the concession to break the fast was prescribed so the count could be completed later.","anchor":"أي تتموا عدة ما أفطرتم فيه وهي أيام السفر والمرض بالقضاء إذا أقمتم وبرأتم"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another possibility is completing the month's count: people without an excuse complete it then, while the sick and travelers complete it at another time.","anchor":"ويحتمل أن يكون معناه ولتكملوا عدة الشهر لأنه مع الطاقة وعدم العذر يسهل عليه إكمال العدة"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكْمِلُوا۟ ٱلْعِدَّةَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"Those who argue Ramadan is never shorter say the command requires an undiminished full count; Tabrisi answers that the required count may be twenty-nine or thirty days, or that the wording refers to making up missed days.","anchor":"أن المراد أكملوا العدة التي وجب عليكم صيامها"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا هَدَىٰكُمْ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In the Imāmī school, this refers to the takbīr on the night of Eid al-Fiṭr after Maghrib, ʿIshāʾ, dawn, and the Eid prayer.","anchor":"المراد به تكبير ليلة الفطر عقيب أربع صلوات المغرب والعشاء الآخرة والغداة وصلاة العيد على مذهبنا"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا هَدَىٰكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās and others interpret it as saying the takbīr on Eid day.","anchor":"وقال ابن عباس وجماعة التكبير يوم الفطر"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا هَدَىٰكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is to magnify God for guiding people to the religious laws.","anchor":"وقيل المراد به ولتعظموا الله على ما أرشدكم له من شرائع الدين"},{"verses":["2:185"],"words":["وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The verse's close means that people should thank God for His blessings.","anchor":"أي لتشكروا الله على نعمه"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:200","rows":[{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["قَضَيْتُم مَّنَٰسِكَكُمْ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qaḍāʾ fundamentally means deciding a matter firmly; it can mean finishing rites, completing an act, decisively announcing something, or issuing a binding judgment.","anchor":"أصل القضاء فصل الأمر على إحكام وقد يفصل بالفراغ منه كقضاء المناسك وقد يفصل بأن يعمل على تمام"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["مِنْ خَلَٰقٍۢ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Khalāq is an allotted share of good, originally a measure or entitlement; another derivation from khuluq makes it the share owed by noble character.","anchor":"والخلاق النصيب من الخير وأصله التقدير فهو النصيب من الخير على وجه الاستحقاق"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["أَشَدَّ ذِكْرًۭا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"أشد is genitive in agreement with the comparison, though it is indeclinable here because its form matches a verb and it is an adjective; it can also be accusative as a verbal noun, with ذكرا as specification.","anchor":"أشد في موضع جلا ولكنه لا ينصرف لأنه على وزن الفعل"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["فِى ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"في الآخرة may attach to the phrase governed by the lām in له; من خلاق is a subject with له as its predicate, and من is extra. Alternatively, في الآخرة is an adverbial circumstantial phrase.","anchor":"في الآخرة الجار والمجرور يتعلق بما يتعلق به اللام"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["فَإِذَا قَضَيْتُم مَّنَٰسِكَكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The phrase means after performing or finishing the rites. Mansak can mean a place of worship, so the phrase covers completing what is due there, or a verbal noun pluralized because rites contain many acts and utterances.","anchor":"المناسك: جمع المنسك والمنسك يجوز أن يكون موضع النسك"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["فَٱذْكُرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One view takes the commanded remembrance as the takbīr specific to the days of Minā, the recommended remembrance of those days.","anchor":"أن المراد به التكبير المختص بأيام منى لأنه الذكر المرغب فيه المندوب إليه في هذه الأيام"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["فَٱذْكُرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A second view takes it as all supplications at those sacred stations, where prayer is better than elsewhere.","anchor":"أن المراد به سائر الأدعية في تلك المواطن لأن الدعاء فيها أفضل منه في غيرها"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["كَذِكْرِكُمْ ءَابَآءَكُمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو جعفر الباقر","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Jaʿfar al-Bāqir reports that pilgrims used to gather after the rites to recount their ancestors' boasts, deeds, and past exploits; God directed them to remember Him instead.","anchor":"ما روي عن أبي جعفر الباقر ع أنهم كانوا إذا فرغوا من الحج يجتمعون هناك ويعدون مفاخر آبائهم ومآثرهم"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["أَوْ أَشَدَّ ذِكْرًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan and Qatāda say to remember God's favors even more, since His blessings exceed those of ancestors and He bestowed their virtues as well as ours; this explains comparison of the obligatory remembrance with a lesser one.","anchor":"على ذلك بأن يذكروا نعم الله ويعدوا آلاءه"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["كَذِكْرِكُمْ ءَابَآءَكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عطاء","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAṭāʾ instead says to seek help and refuge in God as a child turns to and repeatedly calls for its father; Tabrisi prefers the preceding explanation.","anchor":"وقيل معناه واستغيثوا بالله وافزعوا إليه كما يفزع الصبي إلى أبيه في جميع أموره"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["فَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"People at those sacred places fall into groups; one group asks only for worldly benefits and has no share of good in the afterlife because it does not believe in resurrection.","anchor":"بين سبحانه أن الناس في تلك المواطن أصناف فمنهم من يسأل نعيم الدنيا ولا يسأل نعيم الآخرة لأنه غير مؤمن بالبعث"},{"verses":["2:200"],"words":["مِنْ خَلَٰقٍۢ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In this context, no khalāq means no substantial or abundant share of good in the Hereafter.","anchor":"وما له في الآخرة من خلاق"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:219-220","rows":[{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Kufans count two verses across 2:219–220 and treat تتفكرون as a verse ending; the other regional count has one verse and does not count that word as a verse ending.","anchor":"آيتان في الكوفي وآية واحدة فيما عد الكوفي تتفكرون آية وتركها غيره"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["إِثْمٌۭ كَبِيرٌۭ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أهل الكوفة غير عاصم","stance":"reports","claim":"Kufan readers other than ʿĀṣim read إثم كثير with thāʾ, while the other readers use bāʾ and read إثم كبير.","anchor":"قرأ أهل الكوفة غير عاصم إثم كثير بالثاء والباقون بالباء"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["قُلِ ٱلْعَفْوَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو عمرو","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿAmr alone reads العفو in the nominative; the other readers use the accusative.","anchor":"وقرأ أبو عمرو وحده قل العفو بالرفع والباقون بالنصب"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["إِثْمٌۭ كَبِيرٌۭ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو علي","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿAlī supports كبير because كبير contrasts with صغير, while كبير denotes a grave sin; Qur'anic examples use صغير and كبير and call grave sins كبائر. The comparison أكبر also supports كبير rather than كثير.","anchor":"حجة من قرأ بالباء أن يقول الباء أولى لأن الكبر مثل العظم ومقابله الصغر"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["إِثْمٌۭ كَبِيرٌۭ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The كبير reading is supported by Qur'anic wording about every small and great matter being recorded and by references to major sins.","anchor":"وقد استعملوا في الذنب إذا كان موبقا الكبيرة","mentions":["54:53","4:31","42:37"]},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["إِثْمٌۭ كَبِيرٌۭ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The كثير reading is supported by the following verse's account of Satan causing enmity and obstructing prayer and remembrance through wine and gambling, and a report that the Prophet cursed ten involved with wine.","anchor":"وجه قراءة من قرأ بالثاء أنه قد جاء فيهما إنما يريد الشيطان أن يوقع بينكم العداوة والبغضاء"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["إِثْمٌۭ كَبِيرٌۭ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The argument for كثير cites the Qur'anic description of Satan's effects through wine and gambling.","anchor":"إنما يريد الشيطان أن يوقع بينكم العداوة والبغضاء","mentions":["5:91"]},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْخَمْرِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A Prophetic report curses ten wine-related parties: buyer and recipient, presser and commissioner, server and requester, carrier and recipient, and the consumer of its price.","anchor":"لعن الرسول في الخمر عشرة مشتريها والمشتراة له وعاصرها والمعصورة له وساقيها والمستقي لها"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"For accusative العفو, ما ذا is one interrogative expression and ماذا ينفقون functions like ما ينفقون, asking what they spend; the answer is accusative.","anchor":"أن قولهم ماذا يستعمل على ضربين أحدهما"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The single-expression analysis is illustrated by the idiom عما ذا تسأل and a poem asking ماذا بال نسوتكم, meaning ما بال نسوتكم.","anchor":"قول العرب عما ذا تسئل أثبتوا الألف في ما لما كان ما مع ذا بمنزلة اسم واحد"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["قُلِ ٱلْعَفْوَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"For nominative العفو, ذا means الذي, so the question means what is it that they spend; العفو answers as the predicate of an omitted subject.","anchor":"أن يجعل ماذا على الضرب الآخر فيكون تقديره ما الذي ينفقون فجوابه العفو على أن يكون خبر مبتدأ محذوف"}]}
{"loc":"TABRISI:2:219-220#2","rows":[{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The question about what God sent down is cited as a parallel for reading ذا as a relative pronoun.","anchor":"ماذا أنزل ربكم قالوا أساطير الأولين","mentions":["16:24"]},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Sībawayh allows ذا to mean الذي only in this construction; the Kufans permit it elsewhere and cite poetry and Moses' question, but Tabrisi rejects their evidence because the quoted phrases may be circumstantial expressions.","anchor":"سيبويه لا يجوز أن يكون ذا بمنزلة الذي"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["مَاذَا يُنفِقُونَ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"The Kufan evidence from Moses' question does not establish a relative-clause use, since بيمينك may be a circumstantial phrase.","anchor":"يجوز أن يكون ظرفا في موضع الحال","mentions":["20:17"]},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْخَمْرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Khamr derives from covering: foliage, a head covering, a concealing crowd, something mixed into a disease, and covering a vessel all illustrate the root.","anchor":"أصله الستر والخمر ما واراك"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْخَمْرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"كثير","stance":"reports","claim":"The poet Kathīr uses مخامر for an affliction that mingles or remains mixed in, illustrating the root sense of khamr.","anchor":"كثير:
هنيئا مريئا غير داء مخامر لعزة"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْخَمْرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A small palm-fiber prayer mat is called khumra because it covers the face from the ground during prostration.","anchor":"كان النبي يسجد على الخمرة"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْخَمْرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjāj recounts that Abū al-Aswad al-Duʾalī realized an intoxicant sold under another name was wine's sibling; he cited a poem saying both were nursed by the same mother.","anchor":"قال الزجاج وقد لبس على أبي الأسود الدؤلي"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْمَيْسِرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Maysir is gambling, named from yusr because the winner's share becomes due; the gambler is called yāsir because lots determine what is owed.","anchor":"من اليسر وهو وجوب الشيء لصاحبه"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْمَيْسِرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another derivation links maysir to division: whatever is divided is yassartahu; yāsir and maysir can also name the camel being divided.","anchor":"وقيل أخذ من التجزئة لأن كل شيء"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["ٱلْمَيْسِرِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A further derivation connects maysir to ease, since people joined to make sharing the camel easier, though they did so by gambling.","anchor":"وقيل أخذ من اليسر وهو السهولة"},{"verses":["2:219"],"words":["قُلِ ٱلْعَفْوَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-ʿafw means increase or surplus, as in the description of a people increasing in number.","anchor":"العفو مأخوذ من الزيادة ومنه قيل حتى عفوا"}]}
